  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="hogin-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">הוגין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">hwgyn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">hogin</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant" opt="false">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">עוגין</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʿgyn</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">ʿogin</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="hogin-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>anchor</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ὄγκινος</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="la">
                  <quote>uncinus</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אמר ר' יצחק נמשלו אומות העולם בספינה מה ספינה זו עושים לה תורן ממקום אחד 
                     <app>
                        <lem>והוגנים</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V Ox1 Ox2">והוגנין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">הוגבין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">הוגנים</rdg>
                     </app> ממקום אחר</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">83,1</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 997: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Yiśḥaq said: The nations of the world were compared with a ship: Just as this ship, one makes her sailyard from one place [i. e. one sort of material] and her anchors from another. (Cf. Sperber [1986] 139)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 140 [44b: 25]</bibl>; <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Ez 367 [421b: 53]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">והוגנין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 1 Chr 1073 [516d: 3]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">והוגנין</term>); <bibl type="ancient">SekhT 36,30</bibl></note>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ר' שמעון בן לקיש אמר בשר ודם עושה ספינה בתחילה מביא קורות ואחר כך מביא חבלים ואחר כך מביא 
                     <app>
                        <lem>הוגנים</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1 Ox2">הוגים</rdg>
                     </app> ואחר כך מעמיד מוטין</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">12,12</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 111: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Shimʿon ben Laqish said: Flesh and blood [when] he builds a ship; first he brings beams, and then he brings ropes, and then he brings an anchor, and then he places on it sailors. (Cf. Sperber [1986] 142)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Is 450 [397c: 23]</bibl>; <bibl type="ancient">Makh Is 42,5 [126: 28]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">עוגנים</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Not in Krauss. Not clear from the context whether the form is sg. or pl. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow 336a</bibl> explains as Hebr. <term xml:lang="jpa">הגן</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">hgn</term> “ballast, stone”. See Sperber for detailed etymology. Cf. Syr. <term xml:lang="syc">ܐܘܩܝܢܐ</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾwqynʾ</term> (<bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, SL 20a</bibl>).</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sperber (1986)</title>
                  <citedRange>139</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
